WEBVTT

00:01.350 --> 00:03.390
<i>Previously on</i> Captain Tsubasa...<i></i>

00:03.730 --> 00:06.020
<i>Tsubasa and the football club of Nankatsu Elementary</i>

00:06.020 --> 00:09.480
<i>have started their special training
under the direction of Roberto.</i>

00:10.150 --> 00:14.660
<i>For winning the tournament,
you'll have to be friends with the ball.</i>

00:14.660 --> 00:17.330
<i>Be it at school, while eating lunch,</i>

00:17.330 --> 00:19.910
<i>you have to be with it anytime, anywhere.</i>

00:21.250 --> 00:23.790
<i>So, in order to win against Wakabayashi,</i>

00:23.790 --> 00:27.170
<i>Tsubasa and his friends are hard at practice today too.</i>

00:28.500 --> 00:30.510
Over here!

00:30.510 --> 00:31.460
Pass!

00:31.460 --> 00:33.220
Pass the ball to me!

00:34.590 --> 00:35.890
Misaki!

00:37.180 --> 00:38.560
I won't let you!

00:43.270 --> 00:45.400
Nice, Misaki!

00:48.150 --> 00:48.900
All good.

00:50.280 --> 00:51.400
Tarou!

00:51.940 --> 00:53.740
I have finished my painting.

00:53.740 --> 00:55.610
It's almost time to leave.

00:57.030 --> 00:58.990
Are you really going away?

00:58.990 --> 01:01.580
It's been only a month since
you've transferred here.

01:01.580 --> 01:05.000
Can't you at least stay here
until the next school tournament?

01:05.000 --> 01:08.750
We'd be sure to win if you were here.

01:08.750 --> 01:11.800
It can't be helped.
It's about my father's work.

01:11.800 --> 01:13.010
Oh, come on...

01:13.010 --> 01:14.090
Tarou!

01:16.090 --> 01:18.090
Well, everyone. Take care!

01:19.970 --> 01:21.930
You take care too!

01:21.930 --> 01:23.060
- See you!
- Come visit again!

01:24.100 --> 01:25.890
Misaki Tarou...

01:25.890 --> 01:27.900
I really feel bad for him.

01:27.900 --> 01:30.730
I understand that his father is a painter
who travels around the country,

01:31.440 --> 01:35.740
but he had to transfer schools
over thirty times just in elementary school.

01:35.740 --> 01:39.030
If that's how it goes,
he won't really be able to make friends.

01:53.130 --> 01:58.720
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:53.130 --> 01:58.720
<i>koronde toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:58.720 --> 02:03.390
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:58.720 --> 02:03.390
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

02:04.640 --> 02:09.310
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

02:04.640 --> 02:09.310
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

02:10.190 --> 02:17.900
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

02:10.190 --> 02:17.900
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

02:17.900 --> 02:23.660
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

02:17.900 --> 02:23.660
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

02:23.660 --> 02:32.420
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

02:23.660 --> 02:32.420
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

02:32.420 --> 02:37.970
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

02:32.420 --> 02:37.970
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

02:37.970 --> 02:43.890
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

02:37.970 --> 02:43.890
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:43.890 --> 02:45.560
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:45.560 --> 02:52.770
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:45.560 --> 02:52.770
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:52.770 --> 02:55.780
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Go, our kicks!</i>

02:52.770 --> 02:55.780
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kick o</i>

02:55.780 --> 03:00.200
<i>Leap out into a huge TV</i>

02:55.780 --> 03:00.200
<i>tobidasô dodekai TV</i>

03:14.250 --> 03:14.880
Just...

03:17.170 --> 03:20.260
<b><b>EPISODE 5:
ON THEIR WAY TO THE
INTER-SCHOOL TOURNAMENT</b></b>

03:20.430 --> 03:22.050
Come on, what's the matter?

03:23.010 --> 03:25.430
If you can't even take this ball away me,

03:25.430 --> 03:28.020
you can't even dream of winning
against Shuutetsu at the tournament.

03:33.480 --> 03:34.690
What happened?

03:36.190 --> 03:39.150
- Come on, let's go at it once more.
- Yes!

03:47.660 --> 03:50.210
OOZORA

03:51.330 --> 03:53.750
Mom! I'm back!

03:54.210 --> 03:57.170
Welcome back.
The breakfast is ready.

03:57.170 --> 03:57.670
Okay!

03:59.670 --> 04:00.970
Good morning.

04:00.970 --> 04:02.630
Good morning, Roberto.

04:02.630 --> 04:06.470
I'm sorry that you had to
follow him so early in the morning.

04:06.470 --> 04:07.220
It's no problem.

04:07.810 --> 04:09.890
Really... When it's about football,

04:09.890 --> 04:12.060
he can't see anything else.

04:12.060 --> 04:14.100
Just say him no if he asks for something impossible.

04:14.100 --> 04:15.150
It's okay.

04:15.150 --> 04:18.690
It was actually me who proposed
to have an early morning practice.

04:19.650 --> 04:21.070
Oh, is that so?

04:21.070 --> 04:22.700
I guess it's fine then, but...

04:24.030 --> 04:26.160
If it's about my eyes, you don't have to worry.

04:26.160 --> 04:27.120
What?

04:27.120 --> 04:29.740
You've seen my medical report, haven't you?

04:30.790 --> 04:34.250
I'm sorry, I just couldn't help myself.

04:34.290 --> 04:36.040
Sign: MEDICAL DIAGNOSIS REPORT
MR. ROBERTO HONGO

04:39.090 --> 04:41.630
The real reason why I came to Japan was

04:41.630 --> 04:46.050
to be examined by an eye specialist
that Captain Oozora recommended me.

04:46.970 --> 04:49.180
You already know about how it turned out.

04:49.180 --> 04:51.430
I'll never be able to stand in the football field again.

04:53.100 --> 04:56.150
I've already informed Brazil about my intention to retire.

04:56.940 --> 05:00.480
But I have no objections to just being a coach.

05:01.320 --> 05:04.950
Also, I'm having fun teaching Tsubasa now.

05:05.410 --> 05:08.200
Tsubasa is really something.

05:09.030 --> 05:11.540
The more I teach him, the better he gets.

05:11.540 --> 05:14.290
If I keep on training him,
I might even forget about my eyes.

05:16.210 --> 05:17.460
Roberto...

05:18.710 --> 05:20.750
I'm not really forcing myself.

05:23.260 --> 05:25.300
I'm off!

05:33.980 --> 05:35.350
Excuse me.

05:44.070 --> 05:46.780
Don't go that way!

05:46.780 --> 05:49.030
Big news! Big news!

05:49.030 --> 05:52.950
I have to tell everyone right away.

06:01.290 --> 06:02.170
All right!

06:27.450 --> 06:29.240
I can't take this!

06:33.410 --> 06:36.370
So, we will start our first class.

06:36.910 --> 06:38.870
In the previous lesson,

06:38.870 --> 06:41.710
I had everyone to pick a book
they like from the library.

06:41.710 --> 06:43.630
However, some of you...

06:43.630 --> 06:46.460
<i>I knew Manabu would be late.</i>

06:46.460 --> 06:49.130
<i>He just sucks at dribbling.</i>

06:50.890 --> 06:53.510
Ishizaki! Tsubasa!
I've got some big news!

06:59.770 --> 07:01.770
That idiot...

07:04.270 --> 07:06.860
Are you saying that Shuutetsu Elementary
will have a practice match?

07:06.860 --> 07:08.280
There's no doubt about it.

07:08.280 --> 07:12.450
While returning home yesterday,
I ended up going all the way to Mizukoshi Elementary.

07:12.450 --> 07:16.540
The guys from the Mizukoshi Elemantary's
football club were talking about

07:16.540 --> 07:19.910
a practice match with Shuutetsu after school today.

07:20.580 --> 07:23.590
Wait, have really gone as far as Mizukoshi Elementary?

07:23.590 --> 07:25.550
It's on the other side of town.

07:25.550 --> 07:27.090
I had no choice.

07:27.090 --> 07:30.220
The ball just didn't want to listen to me.

07:30.220 --> 07:34.510
But thanks to that,
I got to learn about the practice match.

07:35.350 --> 07:37.390
Let's go and check it, Tsubasa.

07:37.390 --> 07:40.480
The inter-school tournament is soon,
isn't this a good opportunity?

07:40.480 --> 07:41.600
Yeah!

07:41.600 --> 07:45.480
<b>PRIVATE SHUUTETSU ELEMENTARY SCHOOL</b>

07:45.480 --> 07:47.980
<b>SHUUTETSU FOOTBALL STADIUM</b>

07:50.070 --> 07:52.360
Wow, so this is Shuutetsu's field.

07:58.240 --> 08:02.620
This really is a prestigious school.
They are using such a nice field.

08:02.620 --> 08:04.630
- Go!
- Do your best!

08:04.630 --> 08:06.500
Go, Kurata!

08:08.760 --> 08:10.670
It has already started.

08:11.380 --> 08:14.180
Oh, the goalkeeper isn't Wakabayashi.

08:14.180 --> 08:15.010
What?

08:15.850 --> 08:17.510
You are right.

08:17.510 --> 08:20.640
Wakabayashi won't be playing in this match.

08:21.770 --> 08:22.810
Urabe!

08:22.810 --> 08:25.860
I see... Nishigaoka Elementary is
here to oversee the match as well.

08:25.860 --> 08:28.440
Do you know why
Wakabayashi won't be playing?

08:29.730 --> 08:33.860
I hear that he's not even going to school
and is practicing hard every day at his home.

08:33.860 --> 08:34.950
Practicing hard?

08:34.950 --> 08:38.910
Apparently, conceding goals to you
has been a great shock for him.

08:39.660 --> 08:44.330
Well, even without Wakabayashi,
they'll easily win against an opponent like Mizukoshi.

08:46.630 --> 08:49.250
The score is 3-0 even though
they are still in the first half!

08:49.250 --> 08:52.380
Mizukoshi isn't supposed to be such a weak team.

08:52.380 --> 08:55.640
Shuutetsu is strong as usual.

08:55.680 --> 08:57.760
Come on, Mizukoshi Elementary!

08:57.760 --> 08:59.810
Just do your best!

09:04.520 --> 09:05.730
All right, he got it!

09:05.730 --> 09:08.150
He's wide open!
Just keep on going like that.

09:10.190 --> 09:10.690
<i>I got this!</i>

09:22.080 --> 09:23.790
<b>Takasugi Shingo.</b>

09:23.790 --> 09:27.750
He's the center-back who
protects Shuutetsu's goal
along with Wakabayashi.

09:29.750 --> 09:31.750
Take this long pass!

09:31.750 --> 09:33.090
Nice pass!

09:35.300 --> 09:39.890
He's the playmaker. Izawa Mamoru, the midfielder.

09:39.890 --> 09:41.100
I'll take it back!

09:45.140 --> 09:46.270
Run, Taki!

09:50.020 --> 09:54.190
The one who runs along the wings
is Shuutetsu's forward, Taki Hajime.

09:58.320 --> 09:59.700
Kisugi, I'm leaving it to you!

10:00.530 --> 10:02.370
All right, leave it to me!

10:04.910 --> 10:09.460
And lastly, the center forward, Kisugi Teppei.

10:12.380 --> 10:13.630
<b>SHUUTETSU: 4 - MIZUKOSHI: 0</b>

10:13.630 --> 10:16.630
They call them "Shuutetsu Quartet".

10:16.630 --> 10:18.640
<b>SHUUTETSU QUARTET</b>

10:18.640 --> 10:23.010
Shuutetsu didn't win the nationals
just thanks to Wakabayashi.

10:23.010 --> 10:24.890
They won because those guys were there.

10:24.890 --> 10:28.690
Damn it!
Shuutetsu is as strong as ever this year too!

10:28.690 --> 10:30.730
They scored the fourth goal in the blink of an eye.

10:30.730 --> 10:33.150
Winning against them is impossible after all.

10:33.230 --> 10:37.150
Shuutetsu Elementary is great!
They're worth beating!

10:37.150 --> 10:38.400
What?!

10:38.400 --> 10:40.110
Tsubasa?!

11:13.110 --> 11:13.820
Next!

11:17.240 --> 11:18.240
Next!

11:19.820 --> 11:20.610
Next!

11:22.370 --> 11:24.740
Next!
Just keep on going.

11:29.250 --> 11:30.620
You're slow!

11:37.340 --> 11:38.630
Come at me!

11:46.890 --> 11:50.270
<i>Tsubasa did say that they were worth beating.</i>

11:50.270 --> 11:52.560
<i>I'd be happy if we could beat them,</i>

11:52.560 --> 11:54.650
<i>but if they attack us like that...</i>

12:01.650 --> 12:03.240
<i>Run, Taki!</i>

12:03.240 --> 12:05.240
<i>Kisugi, I'm leaving it to you!</i>

12:10.000 --> 12:14.080
<i>And they say that Wakabayashi
is still doing some sort of special training. </i>

12:14.920 --> 12:16.000
<i>However...</i>

12:16.590 --> 12:17.880
<i>I'll challenge him!</i>

12:27.390 --> 12:28.680
<i>Not yet!</i>

12:35.440 --> 12:37.440
<i>Go!</i>

12:40.110 --> 12:42.280
<i>We need to work hard too.</i>

12:42.280 --> 12:46.200
<i>If we give up now, we'll have reverted
back to our former selves.</i>

12:46.200 --> 12:47.240
<i>All right!</i>

12:57.630 --> 12:59.920
Come on! Is that all you've got?

13:02.420 --> 13:04.300
That's pretty good.

13:05.430 --> 13:06.550
Come on!

13:10.060 --> 13:11.140
I did it!

13:13.520 --> 13:14.140
How was that?

13:14.560 --> 13:17.650
You've just made some good decisions, Tsubasa.

13:17.650 --> 13:21.860
All right! Let's practice some different curve shots!

13:21.860 --> 13:23.610
Tsubasa! Coach!

13:27.160 --> 13:30.490
You're only teaching Tsubasa, Coach!
That's unfair!

13:30.490 --> 13:32.750
We whined a lot yesterday,

13:32.750 --> 13:36.040
but we genuinely want to win against Shuutetsu.

13:36.040 --> 13:37.580
Teach us too!

13:37.580 --> 13:39.630
We'll come every morning.

13:39.630 --> 13:40.670
Guys...

13:42.710 --> 13:43.840
Very well!

13:43.840 --> 13:45.300
Everyone, get into your positions.

13:46.130 --> 13:48.050
You'll undergo some special training until the tournament!

13:48.050 --> 13:49.970
Yeah!

13:56.480 --> 13:57.400
Tsubasa!

13:58.860 --> 14:03.320
You put too much strength in your legs.
Put your strength only at the moment of impact!

14:03.740 --> 14:04.570
Got it!

14:05.150 --> 14:05.780
Okay...

14:08.280 --> 14:08.780
I'll have that.

14:09.870 --> 14:12.870
If you start thinking after you get the ball,
it'll be too late, Oda.

14:12.870 --> 14:13.540
Yes!

14:14.160 --> 14:18.830
Firmly make the leg you're standing on your axis,
then turn around and push it out facing forward.

14:20.250 --> 14:22.750
Firmly stand, turn around and push out.

14:23.340 --> 14:26.220
It's the same as scooping
something up with your hands. Try it.

14:26.220 --> 14:27.340
Yes.

14:27.340 --> 14:31.260
Firmly stand, and like scooping it up...

14:33.220 --> 14:36.140
Well, keep on without giving up.

14:36.140 --> 14:36.980
Okay.

14:39.650 --> 14:40.730
Iwami!

14:41.900 --> 14:43.530
Look around yourself more!

14:48.150 --> 14:50.160
- Faster!
- Okay!

14:50.160 --> 14:51.070
Next!

14:54.830 --> 14:55.660
Next!

15:11.220 --> 15:14.560
Firmly stand, and like scooping it up...

15:15.890 --> 15:16.890
It got up!

15:25.650 --> 15:26.570
Tsubasa!

15:49.720 --> 15:51.470
Finally, tomorrow's the day.

15:54.220 --> 15:55.180
This feels so good.

16:02.600 --> 16:03.610
All right!

16:03.610 --> 16:05.770
Firmly stand,

16:05.770 --> 16:07.980
and like scooping it up with my hands...

16:15.950 --> 16:17.990
I did it!

16:21.830 --> 16:22.870
Good morning!

16:25.130 --> 16:27.500
Even Manabu isn't late to school anymore.

16:27.500 --> 16:30.130
Everyone seems to be able to easily make it on time.

16:30.130 --> 16:34.390
This is the result of our practices.
It's all thanks to our coach.

16:34.390 --> 16:36.640
Let's win tomorrow for sure.

16:36.640 --> 16:39.470
The guys from the football club
are really in high spirits.

16:39.470 --> 16:42.100
They always used to give up without even trying.

16:42.100 --> 16:44.980
They say that they'll win this year.

16:44.980 --> 16:47.900
I hear that they are practicing late
until they can't see the ball anymore.

16:47.900 --> 16:49.400
Wow!

16:49.400 --> 16:52.900
Still, it's useless
to come to school while dribbling.

16:52.900 --> 16:54.910
They just like to show off.

16:54.910 --> 16:55.910
- Hey you!
- Ouch!

16:55.910 --> 16:59.290
I won't forgive you
if you make fun of the football club.

16:59.290 --> 17:01.160
It's the Boss of the cheering squad!

17:05.670 --> 17:08.210
He looks so cool today.

17:10.210 --> 17:14.010
The inter-school tournament will start tomorrow,
so we practice until day's end.

17:14.010 --> 17:15.180
All right!

17:15.180 --> 17:17.550
Put all of your efforts into this!

17:17.550 --> 17:20.010
Even that lousy football club is at it.

17:20.010 --> 17:22.560
This year we'll win for what it takes!

17:22.560 --> 17:24.390
Mr. Principal,

17:24.390 --> 17:27.190
students are motivated more than ever.

17:28.730 --> 17:29.820
Hey...

17:29.820 --> 17:33.110
<i>Even the Nankatsu cheering squad is fired up.</i>

17:33.110 --> 17:34.700
Tsubasa!

17:34.700 --> 17:35.660
What?

17:35.660 --> 17:38.910
Boss, it's enough with the Tsubasa.

17:38.910 --> 17:41.740
We have to cheer on other clubs too!

17:41.740 --> 17:42.950
Don't you dare!

17:42.950 --> 17:44.830
Are you going up against me?

17:44.830 --> 17:46.250
It's a waste of time.

17:46.250 --> 17:48.210
Come on, get back to work!

17:48.840 --> 17:50.090
Hurry up!

17:50.090 --> 17:54.050
Hooray... Hooray... Tsubasa!

17:54.050 --> 17:55.430
Can't hear you!

17:55.430 --> 17:59.390
Hooray... Hooray... Tsubasa!

18:05.270 --> 18:07.690
Is Tsubasa going to play as goalkeeper?

18:07.690 --> 18:09.610
Listen to me Tsubasa!

18:09.610 --> 18:12.650
This is my last lesson
before the inter-school tournament.

18:13.480 --> 18:14.650
Get ready!

18:16.400 --> 18:18.160
Will coach shoot?

18:24.750 --> 18:26.040
So fast...

18:26.040 --> 18:28.170
It's impossible to stop.

18:28.170 --> 18:31.500
What's up Tsubasa?
At least try to react!

18:32.840 --> 18:34.130
Once more!

18:37.050 --> 18:37.930
Again!

18:39.180 --> 18:42.810
Tsubasa can't seem
to touch that ball.

18:42.810 --> 18:46.310
We're coached by an extraordinary man.

18:46.310 --> 18:47.810
<i>Incredible!</i>

18:47.810 --> 18:49.650
<i>These are the shots</i>

18:49.650 --> 18:50.900
<i>of a real pro!</i>

18:58.910 --> 19:02.780
These shots are definitely unstoppable!

19:04.990 --> 19:06.330
<i>I've got it!</i>

19:06.330 --> 19:08.160
<i>I've understood the purpose of this!</i>

19:09.790 --> 19:11.130
How about another?

19:12.750 --> 19:13.630
Okay!

19:15.050 --> 19:17.130
<b><b>26TH SHUUTETSU ELEMENTARY - NANKATSU ELEMENTARY
INTER-SCHOOL TOURNAMENT</b></b>

19:17.130 --> 19:19.630
Thank you very much!

19:22.430 --> 19:24.680
Captain's still absent.

19:24.680 --> 19:27.100
Is he fine? We have a game tomorrow.

19:27.100 --> 19:31.860
What? We're up against Nankatsu
who was stuck with 30 to 0.

19:31.860 --> 19:35.230
We'll easily win if we just mark that Tsubasa guy

19:35.230 --> 19:37.190
who scored a goal against our captain.

19:37.190 --> 19:39.780
I agree it'll be easy.

19:41.990 --> 19:44.160
Very well, congratulations!

19:44.160 --> 19:45.990
Tomorrow's the big day.

19:46.450 --> 19:48.370
You did your best.

19:48.370 --> 19:50.250
Go home and get some rest.

19:50.250 --> 19:51.250
Yes, coach!

19:53.000 --> 19:55.750
- I can't wait for tomorrow.
- Me too.

19:55.750 --> 19:57.960
Let's eat some croquettes.

19:57.960 --> 19:59.010
Good idea.

19:59.010 --> 20:01.840
I've managed to do an instep kick today.

20:01.840 --> 20:02.760
Excellent!

20:04.050 --> 20:06.760
<i>We have progressed a lot!</i>

20:06.760 --> 20:10.560
<i>It's all thanks to you Tsubasa!</i>

20:13.770 --> 20:16.190
You seem to have figured out...

20:16.190 --> 20:17.030
What?

20:17.030 --> 20:19.860
why I made you play as a goalkeeper.

20:19.860 --> 20:21.030
Yes.

20:21.740 --> 20:25.700
I've understood which shots are difficult to stop.

20:25.700 --> 20:30.290
For a goalkeeper, some shots are
harder to see than others.

20:30.750 --> 20:33.330
In the end I didn't stop any of them.

20:34.790 --> 20:36.170
Tsubasa.

20:36.170 --> 20:40.470
Maybe it's obvious but
scoring is the essence of the football.

20:40.470 --> 20:43.550
And tomorrow, that scorer,

20:43.550 --> 20:45.890
will be you Tsubasa.

20:45.890 --> 20:48.560
Okay, I promise we'll win tomorrow.

20:48.560 --> 20:50.350
Great!

20:50.350 --> 20:53.810
Show the results
of your training to Wakabayashi.

20:53.810 --> 20:54.940
Okay.

20:54.940 --> 20:57.820
We'll win tomorrow!

21:29.510 --> 21:31.890
<i>Who's that boy?</i>

21:32.850 --> 21:35.020
He dribbles really good...

21:40.320 --> 21:41.940
Another shot!

21:41.940 --> 21:43.320
Come on, Genzo!

21:47.320 --> 21:51.450
Genzo, show me
the results of your training!

22:03.420 --> 22:05.130
Good, that's perfect!

22:06.130 --> 22:07.760
Incredible...

22:07.760 --> 22:10.100
He stopped two shots at a time

22:10.100 --> 22:11.260
from high-school students.

22:13.890 --> 22:15.850
<i>I can't wait for the inter-school tournament</i>

22:16.600 --> 22:18.020
<i>Oozora Tsubasa!</i>

22:39.040 --> 22:44.920
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:39.040 --> 22:44.920
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.920 --> 22:50.930
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.920 --> 22:50.930
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.930 --> 22:56.940
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.930 --> 22:56.940
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.940 --> 23:03.070
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.940 --> 23:03.070
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.070 --> 23:09.160
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.070 --> 23:09.160
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.160 --> 23:15.250
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.160 --> 23:15.250
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.250 --> 23:21.290
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:26.300
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:26.300
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:26.300 --> 23:33.010
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:26.300 --> 23:33.010
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.010 --> 23:38.890
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:38.890 --> 23:45.440
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:38.890 --> 23:45.440
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.610 --> 23:53.950
COMING UP, EPISODE 6 :

23:54.120 --> 23:58.500
KICK-OFF!
NANKATSU vs. SHUUTETSU
